  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Global Ports Safety project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This action seeks to improve maritime safety in twelve global ports identified on the basis of their contribution to the partner countries&#xbf; economies (Bangladesh, Cambodia, Indonesia, Malaysia, the Philippines, Sri Lanka, Thailand and Vietnam), their strategic position along the EU-Asia maritime route and their vulnerabilities to risks. The action shall consider the global ports as nodes between land (inland transport, manufacturing, storages) and sea (maritime transport).It will leverage on the Team Europe expertise in the maritime sector, in particular from France, Poland and at the EU level, to promote safety standards and build local capacities in the Indo-Pacific region.</narrative>
  </description>
